nditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.89,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.55,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.79\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.73,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.82,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.69,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.85,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.76,\n      \"feedback\": \"Conceptually aligns with Patel-type cyanosulfidic access to the valine aminonitrile branch, but rxn_002 is too compressed to count as a well-specified single reaction. The literature route needs staged H2S/HS-, Cu photoredox and 254 nm UV; as written, rxn_002 is only balanced with 2 H2S. rxn_005 is only balanced with 2 H2O and likely needs stronger hydrolysis conditions. Good route conceptually, but under-specified chemically.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_002\",\n        \"rxn_005\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Split rxn_002 into explicit thioamide and photoreduction steps or route directly to the Patel-type aminonitrile branch.\",\n        \"Add Cu(I)/Cu(II), HS-/H2S and 254 nm UV conditions and correct rxn_002 to use 2 H2S.\",\n        \"Annotate rxn_005 with 2 H2O and explicit hydrolysis conditions.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.55,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.79\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.74,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.80,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.68,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.85,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.75,\n      \"feedback\": \"Reasonable if acetone cyanohydrin is treated as stored reservoir material, but the key cyanosulfidic reduction/deoxygenation is still compressed into rxn_002. rxn_002 n